Z||000006||theogre||12-02-2001||10:58 AM||||These saginaw columns are used in allot of GM cars. Just take the dead one with you so you can make sure the new one mounts the same under the dash. Some columns are a little longer than others. some just have extra trim stuck on the bottom end.<P>You might even be able to find a tilt/telescope unit. I've been wanting one of those. I'm not 100% sure those will fit. I haven't been able to go looking for one yet.<P>don't go by the bracket that bolts to the column with 4 short bolts.. That bracket can varry. You just put the Fiero on in it if needed.<P>It's really best to heve the bad one handy for comparison. It's hard to explain it all.||||reg||1
